# One owning library shares mesh storage between every Farm model.
import ../../../packages/dynlex-ui/ui/scene_round_meshes.dl
import ../../../packages/dynlex-ui/ui/scene_surfaces.dl
import ../../../packages/dynlex-ui/ui/scene_solids.dl
import ../../../packages/dynlex-ui/ui/scene_instances.dl

class:
    patterns:
        website farm shape
    members:
        name as a string
        mesh as UI scene mesh

website farm shapes means: the type of (an empty sequence of website farm shape)

class:
    patterns:
        website farm art library
    members:
        shapes as website farm shapes

Farm shape {a value:name} using {UI scene mesh:mesh} means: @intrinsic("construct", website farm shape, the string form of name, mesh)

to get [a website farm art library]:
    set gable to a UI convex prism mesh from [(a UI point at -0.43 and 0.0), (a UI point at 0.43 and 0.0), (a UI point at 0.0 and 0.37)] with depth 0.76
    set shapes to [
        Farm shape "box" using (a UI box mesh with 1 by 1 by 1 segments),
        Farm shape "small sphere" using (a UI sphere mesh with 10 slices and 7 stacks),
        Farm shape "small cone" using (a UI cylinder mesh with top 0.0 bottom 1.0 height 1.0 around 7 sides capped true),
        Farm shape "cylinder" using (a UI cylinder mesh with top 1.0 bottom 1.0 height 1.0 around 10 sides capped true),
        Farm shape "bucket handle" using (a UI torus mesh with radius 0.095 tube 0.01 around 12 slices and 4 sides swept through 180.0 degrees),
        Farm shape "binding" using (a UI torus mesh with radius 1.0 tube 0.08 around 16 slices and 4 sides swept through 360.0 degrees),
        Farm shape "sphere" using (a UI sphere mesh with 16 slices and 12 stacks),
        Farm shape "leaf sphere" using (a UI sphere mesh with 10 slices and 8 stacks),
        Farm shape "cone" using (a UI cylinder mesh with top 0.0 bottom 1.0 height 1.0 around 10 sides capped true),
        Farm shape "torus" using (a UI torus mesh with radius 1.0 tube 0.24 around 12 slices and 7 sides swept through 360.0 degrees),
        Farm shape "gable" using gable,
        Farm shape "water tile" using (a UI box mesh with 5 by 1 by 5 segments),
        Farm shape "rock" using (a UI icosahedron mesh),
        Farm shape "plane" using (a UI plane mesh with 1 by 1 segments),
        Farm shape "selection ring" using (a UI ring mesh with inner 0.34 outer 0.42 around 32 sides),
        Farm shape "route ring" using (a UI ring mesh with inner 0.32 outer 0.4 around 32 sides),
        Farm shape "crop stalk" using (a UI cylinder mesh with top 1.0 bottom 1.0 height 1.0 around 5 sides capped true),
        Farm shape "carrot root" using (a UI cylinder mesh with top 0.0 bottom 1.0 height 1.0 around 9 sides capped true),
        Farm shape "carrot shoulder" using (a UI sphere mesh with 10 slices and 6 stacks),
        Farm shape "grain" using (a UI sphere mesh with 5 slices and 4 stacks)
    ]
    return @intrinsic("construct", website farm art library, a sequence copying shapes)

to get [the Farm shape named] {a value:name} [in] {a pointer to website farm art library:library}:
    for each shape in (library's shapes):
        if shape's name = name:
            return shape's mesh
    require condition false reporting "Unknown Farm shape"
    return a new UI scene mesh
